{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"d79ce72f3ce8d759","name":"card_event_firebomb","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/CovertOp/events/card_event_firebomb","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"FIREBOMB","text":"Deal 5 damage to a unit, excess is dealt to random enemies if you have 2 or more unspent kredits.","flavorText":"Firebombs, also known as incendiary bombs, were used by both the Allied and Axis air forces during WWII. The United States used firebombing tactics as part of their strategic bombing campaign against Axis powers, particularly in Japan. Firebombing involved the use of incendiary bombs to create large-scale fires that inflicted widespread destruction on urban areas and industrial targets. The most notable example of this strategy was the firebombing raids conducted by the US Army Air Forces against Japanese cities, such as Tokyo, which resulted in devastating firestorms. These raids aimed at crippling Japan's industrial capacity, demoralizing the population, and hastening the end of the war.","faction":"USA","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":4,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_firebomb","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_firebomb_title","SourceString":"FIREBOMB","LocalizedString":"FIREBOMB"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_firebomb_text","SourceString":"Deal 5 damage to a unit, excess is dealt to random enemies if you have 2 or more unspent kredits.","LocalizedString":"Deal 5 damage to a unit, excess is dealt to random enemies if you have 2 or more unspent kredits."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_firebomb_history","SourceString":"Firebombs, also known as incendiary bombs, were used by both the Allied and Axis air forces during WWII. The United States used firebombing tactics as part of their strategic bombing campaign against Axis powers, particularly in Japan. Firebombing involved the use of incendiary bombs to create large-scale fires that inflicted widespread destruction on urban areas and industrial targets. The most notable example of this strategy was the firebombing raids conducted by the US Army Air Forces against Japanese cities, such as Tokyo, which resulted in devastating firestorms. These raids aimed at crippling Japan's industrial capacity, demoralizing the population, and hastening the end of the war.","LocalizedString":"Firebombs, also known as incendiary bombs, were used by both the Allied and Axis air forces during WWII. The United States used firebombing tactics as part of their strategic bombing campaign against Axis powers, particularly in Japan. Firebombing involved the use of incendiary bombs to create large-scale fires that inflicted widespread destruction on urban areas and industrial targets. The most notable example of this strategy was the firebombing raids conducted by the US Army Air Forces against Japanese cities, such as Tokyo, which resulted in devastating firestorms. These raids aimed at crippling Japan's industrial capacity, demoralizing the population, and hastening the end of the war."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::CurrentExpansion","isReserved":true,"draftBaseWeight":0.9,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/USA/CandidateArtwork/Summer_24/t_firebomb.t_firebomb","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Alamy Stock Photo","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/FIREBOMB.FIREBOMB","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":390.0,"Y":512.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_firebomb_photo","SourceString":"Incendiary bombs being dropped over the city of Ko